Copy an image in the chat from its right-click menu, in the desktop app.

The desktop app's window has no context menu of its own, so a right-click on
an image in the chat, or on the image open full screen, did nothing.
ImageContextMenu wraps both (ZoomableImage's button and ZoomViewer's image)
in a menu with "Copy image", only in the Electron shell: a browser keeps its
native menu, which can copy the image already and do more.

copyImage redraws the image on a canvas and writes it as a PNG, the one
image type every clipboard takes, so a JPEG, WebP, GIF or SVG copies too.
The PNG goes to the clipboard as a promise, so the write starts inside the
click's user activation, before the image has loaded. A workspace image is
a blob: URL and always copies; a remote one needs CORS headers.

The menu is portalled, but React still bubbles its events to the image's
ancestors, so it stops pointer and key events: otherwise a click on Copy
image starts a pan on the full-screen stage, and an arrow key pages it.
Base: omnigent v0.18.0 (a8676d23e88d), after 0001-0033.
